s there are a lot more  people using it now there's a lot more  money going into it in the venture  capital there are a lot of people who  are skeptics who are now at least trying  it out and then his thoughts in terms of  what other people should be doing as he  said if you put one percent of your  portfolio in it for by diversification  even if it goes to zero which i think is  highly improbable but of course possible  you can always afford to lose one  percent so pretty damn cool to see bill  miller an absolute legend somebody who  is a expert in terms of finding  disruptive technologies that compound at  high growth rates obviously showcased  with his amazon investment and now  coming out and saying look i'm into  bitcoin but i'm not just into bitcoin  i've got almost 50  approximately of my personal portfolio  in the asset i think is a pretty big  boom and obviously that set the internet  on fire when people see somebody like  this doing that right john yeah i think  one thing to note here is one bill is a  legend that's very clear i mean he made  200  uh from the bottom of the market to the  top of the market why the s p only  returned like 80 so he clearly knows  what he's doing he's done for a very  very long time um so that cannot be  taken with a grain of salt but he also  he  bitcoin is 50 of his portfolio it's  obviously a lot of monetary value but  it's also in other  stocks such as microstrategy and mining  companies so he's kind of getting  involved in the whole ecosystem of it  it's interesting because when you read  the headlines and it just says bitcoin  is 50 of his portfolio you literally  think that's in cold storage just  sitting on like a usb  so it is interesting to think his notes  on every investor getting exposure to  the asset i think are right on target  one percent you can't really uh you can  afford to lose one percent no one wants  to lose money but you can afford it so i  think he's uh he's right on the ball  with his comments here i mean i mean  that's wild  50  in amazon 50 in bitcoin that's just wild  for uh someone who's worth that much  money a billionaire to be doing  something like that i think a lot of  people would say that's crazy like  people think of the idea of like hey  conviction helps build wealth and then  diversification helps preserve it and he  has just completely followed the  opposite of that right he says these are  the two things i'm highest convicted on  i think they have the most the most  upside the highest chance of success  there are two things that i really  believe in and i'm gonna go all in and  you have to respect that and ultimately  it sounds like um  the way that quote made it sound was he  bought some bitcoin back in whatever  year was 2017 2016 or no 2014 right yeah  2014 to 200 watched it up to 500 and  continue buying and then he started  buying again at 30 000 so it sounds like  he actually bought a smaller portion of  his portfolio and then it continued to  grow and grow and grow and outside other  positions and now ultimately he's left  with two big things which are bitcoin  related assets and amazon and it's two  things that i think a lot of people have  have a high degree of conviction in  right for these assets to continue to  grow over time so to see someone like  this do that and not just be sitting  there in a diversification of stocks  bonds currencies commodities and all  these different assets mutual funds and  all these different things i think it  tells you a lot about him as an investor  right he is willing to go all in on the  things that he believes in and clearly  two of those things are amazon and  bitcoin  the other piece of i think his approach  is that uh he actually holds this stuff  for a really long time right and  ultimately um if you go back and you  actually listen to the interview that he  did there's a two-part interview that  got put on on youtube one is about  stocks and then one is about uh bitcoin  specifically and the segment about  stocks actually was the more interesting  one to me because it showcases how uh  bill thinks he's one of the clearest  investment thinkers that uh that i think  people can learn from um and  what he talks about in there is he says  look uh let's say facebook as an example  facebook had grown in value and that  value uh many people would have said is  oh they're overvalued right the  multiple's too high etc there's  regulatory risk on uh on the horizon  well he's like but yeah that got priced  in because now the multiple is  compressed the stock has come down some  and so given the risk that they face and  given the health of their business it's  actually like a pretty attractive uh  kind of valuation right he goes through  google same thing and he goes through a  couple of these companies then he  talks about amazon which is obviously  something he knows very well and uh he  talked about how amazon is going through  a high period of capital outflow right  they're outlaying a bunch of capital in  terms of uh all their logistics and  transportation building out all the  warehouses and he compares it to places  like uh walmart where he's like look  walking around for 50 60 years doing  this stuff amazon in a short period of  time is gonna have just as much  warehouse space or a competitive amount  of logistical uh um abilities etc and so  the reason why that's all important is  because then what you get is you  basically end up with a scenario that uh  he's explaining okay they're gonna  outlay a bunch of capital today but  that's gonna drive future cash flow  right and that cash flow is gonna be  high cash flow high margin in the future  so owning it today as a business is  super attractive because they're making  investments today that will pay off in  the future now again whether that  happens or not i think is  ultimately up to up to the market and to  performance and all that but it like the  understanding of how a business actually  operates and and 